// TEST: A Mut Argument Beside An Array A Callback Returned Is Refused (rejects)
// ============================================================================
// Gap G240 / G250, round 4 wave 9 (lane C, C2; Codex design review 5f64f352,
// probe E): `via(get)` returns whatever its callback returns -- here the
// module array g itself -- but the storage walk read a call through a
// function value as returning only its arguments, so `alias` looked fresh and
// `bump(g, alias)` was accepted. A storage-holding result of a call through a
// function value (or of a callee whose return summary is unknown) is now
// UNKNOWN beside a mut argument: refused fail closed (BL4005).
// ============================================================================
type A = Array<Float64 like Idx<2>>
let mut g: A = [2.0, 3.0]
function bump(y: mut A, z: A) -> Float64 = {
    y(0) = 9.0
    z(0)
}
function get(t: Float64) -> A = g
function via(cb: Float64 -> A) -> A = cb(1.0)
let alias = via(get)
let r = bump(g, alias)
// ERROR: BL4005
// ERROR-CONTAINS: could not be traced
// REJECT-AT: lower